<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brihaspati Smriti</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brihaspati Smriti is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> legal text of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dharmashastra">Dharmashastra</a> tradition, attributed to the sage Brihaspati. Compiled or refined during the Gupta period, it dealt with civil and criminal law, property, inheritance and judicial procedure. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narada-smriti">Narada Smriti</a>, it codified law along Brahmanical lines in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>.</p></div>
